  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The proposed redevelopment of the site for housing would be compatible with the character of the residential area and the proposal would not harm the appearance of the street scene or neighbours' living conditions. The development would provide acceptable living conditions, and would accord with the Council's traffic and parking standards. The proposal complies with policies ENV-B.1.1 (New Development), E.1.5 (Development involving Loss of or Changes in Employment Uses), H.1.1 (Location of New Housing Development), H.4.1 (Housing Standards and Guidelines), H.4.2 (Residential Density) and T.1.4 (Car and Cycle Parking and Servicing Facilities For Developments).",
    "Condition : 2 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of five years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 3 - No development shall take place until samples of the materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the hereby permitted have been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority.  Development shall be carried out in accordance with the approved details",
    "Condition : 4 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the flats are occupied.",
    "Condition : 5 - No demolition or construction work shall take place on the site except between the hours of  08.00  to 18.00 on Mondays to Fridays and 08.00 to 13.00 on Saturdays and none shall take place on Sundays and Public Holidays without the prior agreement of the Local Planning Authority.",
    "Condition : 6 - Before commencement of operations, a scheme shall be submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority to cover the following matters:\r\n\r\n(i)\tany external illumination of the site\r\n\r\n(ii)\tmeasures to ensure that all mud and other loose materials are not carried on the wheels and chassis of any vehicles leaving the site; and\r\n\r\n(iii)\tmeasures to minimise dust nuisance caused by the operations and to ensure that no dust or other debris is carried on to the adjoining properties.\r\n\r\nThe scheme so approved should be fully implemented.\r\n",
    "Condition : 7 - The use hereby permitted shall not be begun until details of the arrangements for storing of waste and recycled materials have been submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority.  The arrangements for storing waste and recycled materials shall not be carried out otherwise than in accordance with any approval given and shall be completed before any part of the accommodation hereby permitted is occupied.",
    "Condition : 8 - No development shall take place until full details of both hard and soft landscaping have been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority. Such details shall include, boundary treatment, parking layouts, vehicle access, separate pedestrian access and planting plans, and the scheme shall not be implemented otherwise than in accordance with any approval given.  The details so approved shall be implemented before first occupation of the properties or (in the case of planting ) in the first available planting season after completion of the development.",
    "Condition : 9 - Before development commences details of sightlines at the point of access to the public highway shall be submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority and the development shall be carried out in accordance with the details.",
    "Condition : 10 - A splay of 2.4m x 2.4m shall be provided on each side of the access, the depth measured from the back of the footway and the widths outwards from the edges of the access, and no fence, wall or other obstruction to visibility exceeding 0.6m in height above the surface of the adjoining highway shall be erected within the areas of such splays.",
    "Condition : 11 - Before the development commences details of cycle parking provision in accordance with the Council's Parking Standards shall be submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority and shall be implemented and brought into use prior to first occupation of the new dwellings, and retained permanently.",
    "Condition : 12 - Before the development hereby permitted is commenced a scheme indicating the provision to be made for disabled people to gain access to the ground floor of the flats shall have been submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority.  The agreed scheme shall be implemented before the development hereby permitted is brought into use."
  ],
